8. UNREAL ENGINE 5 C++ CODE PURITY & COMPILATION STANDARDS
========================================================

All generated Unreal Engine 5 C++ must compile cleanly.

Header Include Rules:

• All .h files must include CoreMinimal.h or the specific parent class header.
• The generated reflection header must be the final include in any .h file.
• No includes are allowed below the generated header.

Correct pattern:

#include "CoreMinimal.h"
#include "Subsystems/GameInstanceSubsystem.h"
#include "MySubsystem.generated.h"

API Macro Rule:

All exported UCLASS declarations must include the project API macro.

Example:

class REALMCONVERGENCE_API UMySubsystem : public UGameInstanceSubsystem

Reflection Rules:

Use proper Unreal reflection macros:

• UCLASS(Blueprintable, BlueprintType)
• USTRUCT(BlueprintType)
• UENUM(BlueprintType)
• UFUNCTION(...)
• UPROPERTY(...)

Use FTableRowBase for data table row structs when appropriate.

Memory and Object Safety:

• Use Unreal-managed object ownership.
• Prefer TObjectPtr for UObjects where appropriate.
• Prefer TWeakObjectPtr for weak references.
• Prefer TSoftObjectPtr for asset references.
• Avoid unsafe raw pointer ownership.
• Respect Unreal garbage collection.
• Avoid circular hard references where soft references or IDs are better.

Code Rules:

• No pseudo-code.
• No invalid switch-case syntax.
• No placeholder-only implementations.
• No missing return paths.
• No undefined symbols.
• No impossible include paths.
• No markdown inside source files.
• No plain-text file headers inside source files.
• No deployment notes inside .h or .cpp files.

